  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No person and no sky ascent drawn for 125:17-20. 125:21-28 «الرجس» is not glossed (Al-Muyassar reads it as punishment; the tafsirs word it differently). 127 (Paradise, «دار السلام»): light mood only; no garden, river or gold motif. Light for «يشرح صدره للإسلام», footsteps for «صراط ربك مستقيما», geometric for «وهو وليهم». STAGING v4: c1 (125): the sign of guidance and of misguidance shown on two men in a town by day: the guided man (light robes) gets a soft sparkle on 125:6 and raises his hands on 125:8 (his chest opened to Islam); no plate above him, so his raised hands never point at a light plate; the man in dark robes wrings his hands and lowers his head on 125:15-16 (his chest tight); the simile of climbing into the sky is only a camera tilt to the sky (125:18), nobody ascends. The camera holds on him for 125:24-28 (no gloss on 125:24, as before); no plate there. c2 (126-127): believers in a prayer hall read on 126:7 (the verses detailed for those who remember, footsteps for the straight path); the Home of Peace is not drawn (light plate only, 127:2-5), geometric for 127:6-7, and they pray on 127:8-10 (because of what they used to do). No sujud under a plate."
